[
    {
        "content": "<p>Only function definitions can generalize. Non-function values have exactly one type and annotations can only make the type stricter, not more flexible.</p>\n<p>You can however use _ like this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"CoffeeScript\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nv\">parse_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">const</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Left</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">skip</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">codeunit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">'L'</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">keep</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">digits</span><span class=\"p\">({}))</span>\n\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_right</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_right</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">const</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"o\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Right</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">n</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">skip</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">codeunit</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">'R'</span><span class=\"p\">)).</span><span class=\"nx\">keep</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Utf8</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">digits</span><span class=\"p\">({}))</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Or, define the union once and use it everywhere:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"CoffeeScript\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"nv\">Either</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">[</span><span class=\"nx\">Left</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U64</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Right</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U64</span><span class=\"p\">)]</span>\n\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_line</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Either</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_left</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Either</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"nv\">parse_right</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Parser</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">List</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">U8</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Either</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">_</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 642528359,
        "sender_full_name": "Anton",
        "timestamp": 1795285483
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"361169\">Anton</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/231634-beginners/topic/Open.20Tag.20unions.20on.20parsers/near/642528359\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Only function definitions can generalize. Non-function values have exactly one type and annotations can only make the type stricter, not more flexible.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Ok. I hope this will change in the future. I am not entirely sold on the workarounds. I often skip the type annotations and only add them, if there is a bug with the inferred type and I want to isolate it to one function. So the placeholder <code>_</code>does not help in this situation. Its similar with the \"global type\". It does not help to understand, what a simple function does.</p>\n<p>I will try the different workarounds and see, what will work best.</p>",
        "id": 642633130,
        "sender_full_name": "Oskar Hahn",
        "timestamp": 1795334936
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"496321\">Oskar Hahn</span> has marked this topic as resolved.</p>",
        "id": 642633141,
        "sender_full_name": "Notification Bot",
        "timestamp": 1795334948
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>Ok. I hope this will change in the future</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I suspect that it's like this for a good reason, I will do some research.</p>",
        "id": 642633395,
        "sender_full_name": "Anton",
        "timestamp": 1795335112
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yeah it'll be like this for 0.1.0 - I have some ideas for things to try, but it's a tricky problem because of what constants compile to in Roc, so the restriction means we don't have to solve it right now <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span></p>",
        "id": 642676985,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Feldman",
        "timestamp": 1795364084
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Incidentally I have run into this as well while working on updating my fork of roc-pg. Basically, my solution has just been to add thunks everywhere. I was hoping the thunks wouldn't make it to the public API but alas: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"CoffeeScript\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nv\">rows</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Pg</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Cmd</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">new</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"a query\"</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">bind</span><span class=\"p\">([</span><span class=\"nx\">Pg</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Cmd</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">str</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"John\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Pg</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">Cmd</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">u8</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">32</span><span class=\"p\">)])</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">expect_n</span><span class=\"p\">(</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"nv\">name</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Result</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">str</span><span class=\"p\">({})(</span><span class=\"s\">\"name\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">                </span><span class=\"nv\">age</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nx\">Result</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">u8</span><span class=\"p\">({})(</span><span class=\"s\">\"age\"</span><span class=\"p\">),</span>\n<span class=\"w\">            </span><span class=\"p\">}.</span><span class=\"nx\">Result</span><span class=\"p\">,</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"nx\">send</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"nx\">client</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 642748731,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryce Miller",
        "timestamp": 1795400715
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"522634\">Bryce Miller</span> has marked this topic as unresolved.</p>",
