    {
        "content": "<p>Does anyone have any ideas for ways to make this API nicer for 0.1?</p>",
        "id": 642748949,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryce Miller",
        "timestamp": 1795400824
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>e.g., given that Roc has a feature freeze right now, is there a different way I can design the query parsing API that doesn't require thunks?</p>",
        "id": 642749088,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryce Miller",
        "timestamp": 1795400878
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>(Thunks aside, it's looking like I should have roc-pg ready to go soon!)</p>",
        "id": 642751954,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryce Miller",
        "timestamp": 1795402471
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hey Bryce! <span aria-label=\"smiley\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f603\" role=\"img\" title=\"smiley\">:smiley:</span></p>",
        "id": 642753059,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Feldman",
        "timestamp": 1795402938
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have a WIP solution for this case</p>",
        "id": 642753102,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Feldman",
        "timestamp": 1795402961
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it's a fairly invasive change, but it turns out that (unless the implementation runs into something unexpected), we can change the restriction from \"no type variables allowed in constants\" to just \"no <code>where</code> clauses allowed in constants\" without any major downside</p>",
        "id": 642753243,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Feldman",
        "timestamp": 1795403015
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>and I assume these cases wouldn't need <code>where</code> clauses?</p>",
        "id": 642753292,
        "sender_full_name": "Richard Feldman",
        "timestamp": 1795403039
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The only where clauses I have are on methods within <code>Pg.Client</code>, nothing in the encoding/decoding paths.</p>",
        "id": 642755613,
        "sender_full_name": "Bryce Miller",
        "timestamp": 1795404295
    },
